-- #1111 A-2.13 (#1319 unit 3) — #1377's drain, on all three engines.
--
-- THE SHAPE: this module NAMES one `Cfg` as a type and HOLDS a value of a
-- different `Cfg`.  `useA`'s signature spells armod's `Cfg` (through the
-- re-exporter); `mkZ` is zrmod's `Cfg`, whose type this file never writes and does
-- not need to — `mkZ`'s type comes from zrmod's signature and already carries its
-- origin.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS IS THE CELL THAT PROVES THE FIX IS A SPLIT AND NOT A RELOCATION.  One
-- bare-keyed `recordByNameRef` entry answered BOTH "which `Cfg` does the word
-- `Cfg` on line `useA : Cfg -> Int` mean?" and "which record describes `mkZ`?", so
-- whichever mechanism decided that single entry necessarily gave both the same
-- answer and a module in this shape could not get both right.  Unit 2's per-module
-- scope decision is still what answers the FIRST question (it is a spelling
-- question, and `entry` did import armod's `Cfg` by name); unit 3 gives the SECOND
-- question its own key.  A fixture that only exercised one of the two questions
-- would pass under either mechanism alone.
--
-- Before, measured first-hand on a binary cold-built from `main` @ e93d38d9, in
-- BOTH import-clause orders: exit 1, `Type mismatch: Cfg vs Cfg — … 'zrmod' …
-- 'armod'` plus `Field 'beta' does not belong to record 'Cfg'`.  Before unit 2 it
-- was a coin flip on clause order (`remod` first → the correct `5`; `zrmod` first →
-- exit 1) — which is why order-invariance is pinned separately at
-- `test/import_order_fixtures/record-named-type-vs-held-value-invariant/`, and why
-- THAT row must stay green: a fix that accepts one ordering and refuses the other
-- has restored the coin flip.  Neither cell subsumes the other — this one would
-- stay green under a regression that made only one ordering wrong, and that one
-- would stay green under a regression that made BOTH wrong.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS IS ALSO THE CELL THAT MEASURES THE DECLARING-MODULE CONJUNCT of the
-- identity match, and it is the only one that does.  Stubbed, not argued: with
-- the module comparison dropped (match on the owning TYPE NAME alone) this cell
-- goes RED with the two diagnostics above, while `…_value_only/` and
-- `…_bystander/` both stay GREEN.  The bystander covers the other conjunct.
--
-- Hand-derived correct answer, independent of any engine: `useA c = 0` by
-- definition and `mkZ.beta = 5`, so `5`.
import remod.{Cfg, mkA}
import zrmod.{mkZ}

useA : Cfg -> Int
useA c = 0

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (intToString (useA mkA + mkZ.beta))
